   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Travelling and moving city",
     "texto": [
      "In the world there are **continentes** and **océanos**. A **península** is land surrounded by water on almost all sides.\n\nWhen you travel, the weather can change: a **tormenta**, **niebla** or an **ola de calor**.\n\nA **turista** or a **viajero** visits a place and goes home. Whoever **se muda** changes house and **barrio**, with their **maleta**. You can **echar de menos** the people and your home city.\n\nThe **población** of a city is the people who live in it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Telling a trip: simple past and imperfect",
     "texto": [
      "To tell a trip, use two pasts:\n\n- **Indefinido**: what happened, a finished action: **hubo una tormenta**, **llegamos al puerto**.\n- **Imperfecto**: what the situation was like or what happened often: **hacía mucho calor**, **había niebla**.\n\nThey combine: **cuando llegamos, hacía frío**.\n\nWith **haber**: the simple past is **hubo** and the imperfect is **había**. **Hay** becomes **hubo** for an event, and **había** when describing."
     ],
